# The CN 720's X axis (cmp40m + x.conf, 10 mm screw) with a FANUC alpha-type
# absolute encoder (simulated: host/hw/encf.c) and mturn: the position over
# smart-serial is the absolute one from boot, keeps it over a power cycle,
# and enabling there does not move the axis.
# The shaft (and the encoder on it) is put at 37.25 turns (372.5 mm) and
# the drive reset, so it boots there;
# a hand turns the screw 2.5 turns (+25 mm; the simulated hand sums its
# steps in float, ~2 um short) while the drive is not enabled;
# the drive is reset (power cycle; the shaft keeps its place:
# hv0.sim_keep_pos in fanuc_sim.txt); LinuxCNC enables at the
# position it reads, holds, then jogs 10 mm (5 mm/s for 2 s).
@args --drive tests/abs/mill_x_fanuc.conf --sim tests/abs/fanuc_sim.txt
hv0.sim_upos = 234.04866
run 0.05
reset
run 0.2
sserial0.scale = 10
run 0.05
mturn0.state
mturn0.abs_ok
linrev0.fb_out
hv0.sim_turn = 15.70796
run 3
linrev0.fb_out
reset
run 0.2
sserial0.scale = 10
run 0.05
mturn0.loads
mturn0.abs_ok
linrev0.fb_out
lcncscale 10
lcnc 0 0 397.5
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0 397.5
run 1.5
hv0.sim_dist
fault0.state
fault0.fault
lcnc 1 5
run 2
lcnc 1 0
run 0.5
linrev0.fb_out
mturn0.state
@expect mturn0.state[1] == 1
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[1] == 1
@expect linrev0.fb_out[1] ~ 372.5 0.001
@expect linrev0.fb_out[2] ~ 397.5 0.01
@expect mturn0.loads == 1
@expect mturn0.abs_ok[2] == 1
@expect linrev0.fb_out[3] ~ 397.5 0.01
@expect max|hv0.sim_dist| < 0.05
@expect fault0.state == 1
@expect fault0.fault == 0
@expect linrev0.fb_out[4] ~ 407.5 0.01
@expect mturn0.state[2] == 1
